WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.300
What artists do.

2
00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:03.643
Artists do four things, round and round.

3
00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:06.032
They experience: look, touch, try.

4
00:00:06.192 --> 00:00:08.375
They make: mix, draw, join, build.

5
00:00:08.535 --> 00:00:11.228
They reflect: look back, celebrate, compare.

6
00:00:11.388 --> 00:00:15.521
And they think and work like an artist: have ideas, be brave, make it better.

7
00:00:15.681 --> 00:00:17.260
You did all four this year.

8
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:18.982
A gallery.

9
00:00:19.142 --> 00:00:22.486
A gallery is a place where art is put up for people to see.

10
00:00:22.646 --> 00:00:26.686
The pictures hang in groups: by colour, or by what they are about.

11
00:00:26.846 --> 00:00:29.772
People walk past and compare them, and say what they like.

12
00:00:29.932 --> 00:00:32.022
Your class can make one on a table.

13
00:00:32.722 --> 00:00:33.929
Making it better.

14
00:00:34.089 --> 00:00:38.640
Before a show, artists look at every piece and make one change to make it better.

15
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.193
Not because it was bad.

16
00:00:40.353 --> 00:00:41.839
Nothing you made was bad.

17
00:00:41.999 --> 00:00:44.879
Because an artist can always see one more thing to try.

18
00:00:45.579 --> 00:00:46.647
Looking back.

19
00:00:46.807 --> 00:00:48.850
Your journal holds everything you made.

20
00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:50.310
Look back through it.

21
00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:53.489
Your first line, your first mix, your first pattern.

22
00:00:53.649 --> 00:00:55.135
See how far you came.

23
00:00:55.295 --> 00:01:02.029
That is reflecting, and it is the last thing an artist does, and the first thing before the next picture.
